<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-cefa1.5 — schema type-hygiene pass, Tier B, P4 (epic nexus-cefa1;
    plan of record T2 nexus/plan-schema-type-hygiene-2026-08-12 [22360]).
    Template: aspects-003-type-hygiene.xml (nexus-cefa1.4, P3) — the closest
    sibling for a bare TYPE ... USING with no DROP/SET DEFAULT bracketing
    (neither plans.plan_json nor plans.default_bindings carries a DEFAULT
    per plans-001-baseline.xml:76,85).

    Retires two RDR-152 SQLite-port TEXT columns on nexus.plans, in ONE
    changeset (ONE ALTER TABLE, one table rewrite):

    - plan_json: TEXT NOT NULL -> jsonb NOT NULL, via TYPE jsonb USING
      plan_json::jsonb (plain cast, no NULLIF — NOT NULL stays NOT NULL, and
      the P0 pre-flight found empty_string_count=0 on the only populated
      deployment, so there is no '' value that a NULLIF step would need to
      catch; a plain ::jsonb cast on an empty string would abort the ALTER
      with "invalid input syntax for type json" — column is safe without it
      because that value never occurs, confirmed by the count, not assumed).
    - default_bindings: TEXT NULL -> jsonb NULL, via TYPE jsonb USING
      NULLIF(default_bindings, '')::jsonb (same NULLIF-guard shape as every
      other nullable Tier-B column in this arc — an empty string is not a
      valid jsonb literal, so it must become SQL NULL first).

    NOT NULL is preserved automatically across ALTER COLUMN TYPE on
    plan_json (never touched, no DROP/SET NOT NULL needed); neither column
    carries a DEFAULT to drop or restore.

    ALTER COLUMN TYPE is ordinary DDL (an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE table rewrite),
    not RLS-filtered DML — no FORCE RLS toggle needed, and the changeset
    touches no row via INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.

    EXCLUDED from this pass (recorded per the plan of record's explicit
    deferral, plan-schema-type-hygiene-2026-08-12 §Scope):
    - plans.dimensions / plans.parent_dims stay TEXT. A jsonb conversion of
      `dimensions` would break BYTE-EQUALITY matching: the partial unique
      index `idx_plans_tenant_dimensions ON nexus.plans (tenant_id, project,
      dimensions) WHERE dimensions IS NOT NULL` (plans-001-baseline.xml:104)
      IS the plan-identity constraint, and jOOQ's `PLANS.DIMENSIONS.eq(...)`
      equality lookup in `PlanRepository.getByDimensions`
      (service/src/main/java/dev/nexus/service/db/PlanRepository.java:111)
      compares the caller-supplied dimensions string against the stored
      value verbatim. jsonb round-tripping is NOT byte-identical (key order
      and whitespace canonicalize on write: Postgres stores jsonb object
      keys sorted by key length, then bytewise, never in input order, and
      re-serializes with its own canonical spacing; pinned by
      PlanRepositoryTest.savePlan_planJson_jsonbCanonicalizesWhitespaceAndKeyOrder),
      so a jsonb
      `dimensions` column would silently break both the partial unique index
      semantics (two dimensionally-identical-but-differently-formatted JSON
      strings currently collide on the unique index; canonicalization could
      either newly collide non-identical dimension sets after roundtrip
      normalization, or fail to collide two calls that intended the same
      identity but serialized their JSON differently) and the eq-match
      lookup (a caller re-submitting dimensions in a different key order
      would silently miss a plan that canonical-form jsonb would have
      matched). Converting `dimensions` / `parent_dims` needs its own bead
      and its own dedup audit against the unique index and every
      `PLANS.DIMENSIONS.eq(...)` call site, not a drive-by fold into this
      changeset.

    Data-safety evidence: T2 nexus/schema-hygiene-p0-preflight-2026-08-15
    [22588] (nexus-cefa1.1), cloud (the only populated deployment; this
    box's local substrate is a fresh hermetic pytest engine with no seeded
    data): plans.plan_json total_rows=53, null_count=0,
    empty_string_count=0, invalid_cast_count=0; plans.default_bindings
    total_rows=53, null_count=39, empty_string_count=0,
    invalid_cast_count=0. Every row already holds valid JSON (or SQL NULL
    for default_bindings) — both USING clauses above are confirmed safe on
    live data, not merely reasoned from the writers.

    Consumer audit (nexus-cefa1.5, mirroring nexus-cefa1.2/.3/.4's sweeps —
    full findings: T2 nexus/schema-hygiene-p4-plan-jsonb-audit-2026-08-15):
    jsonb round-trip is NOT byte-identical (key order / whitespace
    canonicalize). Swept every Java and Python consumer of plan_json /
    default_bindings for text-equality or hash comparisons:
    - Java: PlanRepository's ON CONFLICT keys are (tenant_id, project,
      query) — never plan_json / default_bindings. No `.eq(...)` or hash
      call touches either column anywhere in PlanRepository.java or
      PlanHandler.java (grepped; only PLANS.DIMENSIONS.eq exists, and
      dimensions is excluded above, unaffected by this changeset).
    - Python: nexus.plans.match.Match.from_plan_row and
      nexus.plans.scope._infer_scope_tags both `json.loads(...)` the
      content — parsing is canonicalization-immune (key order and
      whitespace do not change the decoded structure). nexus.plans.
      seed_loader's dedup key is `canonical_dimensions_json(dimensions)`,
      the SAME excluded-column identity above, not plan_json.
      nexus.mcp.core's RDR-084 plan-growth auto-save
      (`_do_grow`/`db.plans.save_plan`) upserts on `query`, not plan_json
      content; no plan_json hash or string-equality check gates the save.
      No hashlib / `==` / dedup-by-content call touches plan_json or
      default_bindings anywhere in src/nexus/plans/*.py, src/nexus/mcp/
      core.py, or src/nexus/db/t2/*.py (grepped). CONCLUSION: nothing
      breaks under canonicalization — no fix was required.
    - PlanHandler malformed-JSON validation (this bead, new): plan_json is
      REQUIRED (requireString already rejects null/blank before reaching
      the repository) and, additionally, must now parse as valid JSON — a
      non-JSON string 400s at the handler via the shared
      HttpUtil.rejectMalformedJson helper (extracted from AspectHandler's
      private rejectMalformedJson, nexus-cefa1.4, so this is the SECOND
      caller rather than a third copy). default_bindings is optional; when
      present and non-blank it is validated the same way. A write path
      that bypasses the handler (a direct repository call) still falls
      back to the existing class-22 SQLSTATE 422 branch
      (HttpUtil.sendTypedDbError) as the backstop, same as every prior
      phase in this arc.

    ANALYZE after the rewrite (BUG-0148 invariant, rdr180-16-analyze-
    rewritten-tables precedent, mechanically enforced by
    tests/test_changelog_analyze_lint.py) — the ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE above
    resets nexus.plans's planner statistics.

    Rollback: mirrors aspects-003's document_aspects rollback exactly — a
    bare TYPE TEXT USING col::text cast restores the pre-migration shape
    for free (plan_json's TEXT NOT NULL and default_bindings's nullable
    TEXT, no COALESCE-to-'' needed for either, since neither carried a
    DEFAULT and plan_json's NOT NULL survives the round trip unchanged).

    Ordering: registered after aspects-003-type-hygiene.xml (P3) and before
    the grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block, NOT back in the plans-00N
    family's own section near the top of the changelog — matches the
    master changelog's established convention for every new changeset
    since RDR-156 (catalog-031, telemetry-004, aspects-003 all append near
    the current tail rather than splicing back into their family's
    original block).
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <!-- ── Changeset plans-002-1-type-hygiene ──────────────────────────────── -->
    <changeSet id="plans-002-1-type-hygiene" author="nexus-cefa1.5">
        <comment>
            plans.plan_json TEXT NOT NULL -> jsonb NOT NULL; plans.default_bindings TEXT ->
            jsonb NULL (ONE ALTER TABLE, one rewrite). plans.dimensions / .parent_dims stay
            TEXT — deferred, see header (byte-equality plan-identity index / eq-match).
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
ALTER TABLE nexus.plans
    ALTER COLUMN plan_json TYPE jsonb USING plan_json::jsonb,
    ALTER COLUMN default_bindings TYPE jsonb USING NULLIF(default_bindings, '')::jsonb;

-- BUG-0148 invariant (rdr180-16-analyze-rewritten-tables precedent, mechanically
-- enforced by tests/test_changelog_analyze_lint.py): the ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE
-- above rewrites nexus.plans and resets its planner statistics.
ANALYZE nexus.plans;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="true">
ALTER TABLE nexus.plans
    ALTER COLUMN plan_json TYPE TEXT USING plan_json::text,
    ALTER COLUMN default_bindings TYPE TEXT USING default_bindings::text;

ANALYZE nexus.plans;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
